This is just Dead Island, but with some GRAPHIC differences.
Problem is: it's lazilly made, and it needs SERIOUS patching beforte it's recommended.
The bad:
-Excessive bloom, making everything look WAY too bright and hard to see;
-FORCED Chromatic Aberration (that stays even if you disable it);
-No squirting blood from the neck when you chop a zombie's head off anymore;
-Devs went crazy with the post processing effects (sun glare, bloom, haze, motion blur, etc), and you can't even disable most of them;
-There are WAY more bugs than the classic version, and that was already quite buggy;
-Game isn't very well optimized. Runs good, but requires a WAY better PC then the graphics would suggest. Runs worse then Dying Light, in fact.
The good:
+SLIGHTLY better textures;
+Better character models.
This is LAZY. They just ported the classic game to a new engine, but didn't even bother adjusting settings.  NOT recommended.

Here's a quick summary.
Buy the game if:
- You are a fan of the Dragonball Series;
- You just want something to play every now and again casually;
- You love the Dragonball Power fantasy;
- You are looking to play part in battles you've seen in the show but as your own character;
- You have the hots for Buugirls, because they're so soft and cuddly!
Avoid this game if:
- You are looking for a complicated competetive fighting game;
- You are looking for a MMO experience;
- You are looking for a game to sink 100's of hours into;
- You are interested in good game design;
- You want the feeling of a fair battle where skill matters and not luck;
- You have anger issues and are the owner of expensive equipment that you might smash.
I have played this game alot these past few weeks and I enjoy myself. But I am beginning to hit the wall already with things to do. You need to be willing to get a max rank on everything if you want replayability. Once you have your character sorted out and you are around lvl 85, then things will slow down to a crawl and it becomes a min-maxing grindfest.

